## **Then look at the picture**

### **Secondary Synthesis Ledger and Traction Flow Diagram**

The ledger is the cast of this run. Each row is something that came forward.

* Rows marked **Retained** still point back. Those are the holders.  
* Rows marked **Synthesis Refusal** came forward and do not hold this up. Traction is treated as zero. They are excluded from the scores above.

The Traction Flow Diagram is the same cast as a tree: holders on one branch, refusals on the other. Low-traction holders stay on the holder branch. They are weak. They are not leftover. You do not have to read every note.

### **Uncertainty Table**

This is the leftover of this run, plus two other kinds of openness that are not leftover.

* **Synthesis Refusal** — listed supports that do not point back. Same rows as the isolated lines in the ledger.  
* **Retained Openness** — something that stayed under-specified among the holders. It did not fall out. It also did not close.  
* **Inter-Secondary Clash** — two holders that still hold and do not sit easily together. A clash is not leftover. The row should name the pair.

What never came forward is not on this table. Do not hunt it.

